1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,750
This video shows you how to install smeltr with Docker Compose,

2
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:09,788
as one leader and worker served over HTTPS.

3
00:00:09,788 --> 00:00:12,870
Then you sign in for the first time.

4
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:16,417
Make a folder for smeltr, and go into it.

5
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:21,377
Download the compose file of the release you want.

6
00:00:21,377 --> 00:00:23,350
Here, that's 1.1.0.

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,617
It runs the leader and a worker in one container.

8
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:36,670
The leader serves HTTPS on port 443, with a certificate it signs itself.

9
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:41,870
Everything it keeps goes in one volume, so back that volume up.

10
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:46,070
Two settings go in a file named .env, beside it.

11
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,910
The image, with the release's version.

12
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:53,470
And the address your browser opens, with this machine's name.

13
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:55,004
Start it.

14
00:00:56,520 --> 00:01:00,497
On its first start, smeltr creates an administrator,

15
00:01:00,497 --> 00:01:03,990
and prints a one-time password in its logs.

16
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:04,618
Copy it.

17
00:01:04,618 --> 00:01:07,097
It's shown only this once.

18
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:10,150
Open the leader at its address.

19
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,602
The browser warns you.

20
00:01:11,602 --> 00:01:17,030
The leader signed its own certificate, and the browser doesn't know who signed it.

21
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:19,994
For this first sign-in, go on to the leader.

22
00:01:19,994 --> 00:01:23,910
A later video sets up a certificate your browser trusts.

23
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:28,157
Sign in as admin, with the one-time password.

24
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:32,126
smeltr asks you to choose your own password.

25
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:39,056
Then sign in again, with your new password.

26
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:43,165
Status opens on the fleet.

27
00:01:43,165 --> 00:01:49,070
The standalone worker group has one worker, and its check mark says it's online.

28
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:52,087
Running shows the commit the worker runs.

29
00:01:52,087 --> 00:01:55,910
When you deploy a change, it moves to the new one.

30
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:57,930
Check on learning.

31
00:01:58,130 --> 00:02:03,678
After the first start, where do you find the password for your first sign-in?

32
00:02:08,078 --> 00:02:11,591
In the leader's logs, from its first start.

33
00:02:11,591 --> 00:02:13,906
It's shown only once.

34
00:02:14,806 --> 00:02:18,567
Next, you enroll a worker on another machine.
